            "output": "Title: fzf --tmux not rendering\nURL: https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/issues/4845\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\nSimilar to #4814, running `seq 1 10 | fzf --tmux` sometimes renders correctly, sometimes creates an empty popup and using `ctrl+C` closes the popup and prints `exit status 2` on the original terminal.\n...\nThis started failing when a system upgrade bumped fzf from v0.70.0 to v0.73.1, but rolling back the version of fzf does not fix the issue, so it's possible some other dependency is causing problems.\n...\nTmux version is 3.6b, have tried downgrading to 3.6a but issue still persists.\n...\n> I would recommend to try with a clean zsh/tmux/fzf configuration. For example, without tmux running, run `env -i HOME=$(mktemp -d) zsh`, then start tmux and try `seq 10 | fzf --tmux`.\n...\n> Still get the same behavior with a clean configuration. Steps I took:\n> ```\n> 󰁔 env -i HOME=\"$(mktemp -d )\" zsh\n> This is the Z Shell configuration function for new users,\n> zsh-newuser-install.\n> You are seeing this message because you have no zsh startup files\n> (the files .zshenv, .zprofile, .zshrc, .zlogin in the directory\n> ~). This function can help you with a few settings that should\n> make your use of the shell easier.\n> \n> You can:\n> \n> (q) Quit and do nothing. The function will be run again next time.\n> \n> (0) Exit, creating the file ~/.zshrc containing just a comment.\n> That will prevent this function being run again.\n> \n> (1) Continue to the main menu.\n> \n> --- Type one of the keys in parentheses --- q\n> \n> # export TERM so tmux does not complain about the terminal not supporting clear\n> % export TERM=tmux-256color\n> % tmux new-session\n> ```\n> \n> In this new session the behavior shows up again, sometimes the tmux popup is properly populated, I can pick an option and is output on the original terminal, sometimes the popup is just a blank square and I can only terminate it with ctrl+C.\n...\n> > sometimes\n> \n> Do you mean that if you repeatedly run `fzf --tmux` on the same session, it sometimes works and sometimes doesn't? If so, roughly what percentage of the time does it work?\n> \n> I have no idea what might be causing this. I'd try opening a separate terminal window and comparing the process status when it works versus when it doesn't (e.g. with `ps auxf`). That might provide a clue about what's going on.\n...\n> > Do you mean that if you repeatedly run `fzf --tmux` on the same session, it sometimes works and sometimes doesn't? If so, roughly what percentage of the time does it work?\n> \n> Hard to say, but it fails pretty frequently, maybe it works 20% of the time? This is also running the command on the same session and same pane, sometimes it spawns the popup correctly populated, sometimes it spawns a popup that has nothing at all and can only be terminated via ctrl+C. Another odd thing I just noticed is that the problem happens when I pipe content into `fzf --tmux`, but if I don't pipe it and instead simply run `fzf --tmux` it doesn't fail and correctly shows all files/directories in cwd.\n> \n> \n> \n> > I have no idea what might be causing this. I'd try opening a separate terminal window and comparing the process status when it works versus when it doesn't (e.g. with `ps auxf`). That might provide a clue about what's going on.\n> \n> The result of running `ps auxf` shows there is a subprocess that is apparently not being exec'ed as `fzf`.\n> Working correctly:\n...\n> XXXX 938714 0.0 0.0 1748928 7028 pts/7 Sl+ 15:13 0:00 | | \\_ fzf --tmux\n...\n> XXXX 938727 0.0 0.0 234896 4744 pts/7 S+ 15:13 0:00 | | \\_ tmux display-popup -E -d /home/XXXX/worktrees/fact/fact-operator/ -B -xC -yC -w50% -h50% sh /tmp/fzf-temp-3877436904\n...\n> XXXX 938730 0.0 0.0 1896648 8244 pts/12 Sl+ 15:13 0:00 | \\_ fzf --bind=ctrl-z:ignore --tmux --border=rounded --no-popup --no-height --no-force-tty-in --proxy-script /tmp/fzf-temp-3877436904XXXX 924624 0.0 0.0 8152 6112 pts/10 S+ 15:09 0:00 | \\_ rg fzf\n...\n> \n> Failing:\n...\n> XXXX 1069515 0.0 0.0 1822916 7148 pts/5 Sl+ 15:49 0:00 | | \\_ fzf --tmux\n...\n> XXXX 1069525 0.0 0.0 234896 4628 pts/5 S+ 15:49 0:00 | | \\_ tmux display-popup -E -d /home/XXXX/worktrees/fact/fact-operator/ -B -xC -yC -w50% -h50% sh /tmp/fzf-temp-1374029247\n...\n> ```\n> \n> Particularly, these two lines when fzf --tmux works:\n> ```\n> XXXX 938728 0.0 0.0 232352 3844 pts/12 Ss+ 15:13 0:00 | \\_ sh /tmp/fzf-temp-3877436904\n...\n> XXXX 938730 0.0 0.0 1896648 8244 pts/12 Sl+ 15:13 0:00 | \\_ fzf --bind=ctrl-z:ignore --tmux --border=rounded --no-popup --no-height --no-force-tty-in --proxy-script /tmp/fzf-temp-3877436904XXXX 924624 0.0 0.0 8152 6112 pts/10 S+ 15:09 0:00 | \\_ rg fzf\n> ```\n...\n> vs. these two when it fails:\n> ```\n> XXXX 1069526 0.0 0.0 232352 3916 pts/12 Ss+ 15:49 0:00 | \\_ sh /tmp/fzf-temp-1374029247\n> XXXX 1069527 0.0 0.0 232352 1868 pts/12 S+ 15:49 0:00 | \\_ sh /tmp/fzf-temp-1374029247\n> ```\n> \n> The `/tmp/fzf-temp-*` files seem to be scripts, the contents look the same, being a long list of `export` from my env and ending in the fzf command from the process that works.\n...\n> After updating my system again yesterday the issue seems to have resolved itself, even though the update didn't include fzf or tmux 🤷🏻‍♂️ \n> \n> I have to assume some other subsystem was broken and was fixed without me noticing, I'll re-open if I start experiencing the issue again. Sorry for the noise and thanks for all the help!\n\n---\n\nTitle: Disable tmux popup when already running inside one · Pull Request #4351 · junegunn/fzf\nURL: https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/pull/4351\nPublished: 2025-04-18T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: peikk0\nHighlights:\n# Disable tmux popup when already running inside one\n...\n`tmux popup` doesn't work and immediately returns instead when spawn inside one (`tmux popup tmux popup echo foo` results in an empty popup). For that reason, `fzf --tmux` doesn't work when executed inside a `tmux popup`, for example: \n \n```shell\r\nFZF_DEFAULT_OPTS=--tmux tmux popup 'find . | fzf'\r\n```\r\n \nAnd executing `fzf --tmux` inside `fzf --tmux` (as [`forgit`](https://github.com/wfxr/forgit) does, which was how I ran into this issue) also doesn't work, for example: \n \n```shell\r\nfind . -type d | FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS=--tmux fzf --bind=\"enter:execute(find {} -type f | fzf | xargs less)\"\r\n```\r\n \nA popup can be detected by the absence of the `TMUX_PANE` environment variable, so we can simply disable the `--tmux` mode when it is absent. And it also must be excluded for the exports in `runProxy()` so that the popup can also be detected properly by child processes.\n...\n> Thanks!\n\n- peikk0 head_ref_deleted\n\n- Referenced by issue #4360: tmux run-shell 'fzf --tmux' broken in v0.61.2\n\n- Referenced in commit 2a9c1c0\n...\n> Yesterday, I spent hours guessing which update in my system broke my beautiful popups in `tmux`.\n> Thanks for [reverting this](https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/releases/tag/v0.61.3)!\n\n- Referenced by issue #13: Changing Keybinding Not Working\n\n- Referenced in commit 4c64d7b\n\n---\n\nTitle: There are 0 fzf history in the tmux pop-up.\nURL: https://github.com/tmux/tmux/issues/2752\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n# There are 0 fzf history in the tmux pop-up.\n...\n### Required information \n \nPlease provide the following information: \n \n* tmux version: 3.2a \n* Platform: Darwin i386 \n* $TERM inside and outside of tmux: screen-256color \n \n### Expected \nThe fzf history is displayed in the tmux pop-up. \n \nI tried the following command. \n```bash\r\n$ tmux popup '$(history -r | fzf --layout=reverse --no-sort +m --query \"$LBUFFER\" --prompt=\"History > \")'\r\n```\n...\nThen, the number of pop-up history was 0. \nHow can I get rid of 0 history? \n \n \n\n## Timeline\n...\n> You will need to write the history to a tmp file before you run tmux popup and then point fzf to that file.\n...\n> I've tried so far, but the line selected from the pop-up window is not returned.\n> Could you give me some more advice?\n> ```bash\n> function select-history() {\n> tmux popup 'LANG=C; BUFFER=$(cut -f2 -d\";\" ~/.zsh_history | fzf --layout=reverse --no-sort +m --query \"$LBUFFER\" --prompt=\"History > \"); CURSOR=$#BUFFER'\n> }\n> zle -N select-history\n> bindkey '^f' select-history\n> ```\n...\n> How would it be returned? You will need to have fzf put it in a file and then use that from the shell that opened the popup.\n...\n> The list is displayed for the time being,\n> \n> After selecting an item, the pop-up will be blank.\n> \n\n**\n...\n:18:29\n...\n> Right but I don't know what fzf is meant to do there, but tmux won't send any of its output back to the original shell, you will need to arrange that yourself. Use `popup -E` if you want tmux to close the popup when fzf exits.\n> \n> Why don't you look at some of the existing scripts that use fzf for tmux?\n...\n> Solved.\n> I used `fzf-tmux` which is included in `fzf`.\n> ```bash\n> function select-history() {\n> BUFFER=$(history -n -r 1 | fzf-tmux -p --layout=reverse --no-sort +m --query \"$LBUFFER\" --prompt=\"History > \")\n> CURSOR=$#BUFFER\n> }\n> zle -N select-history\n> bindkey '^f' select-history\n> ```\n> thanks\n\n---\n\nTitle: $FZF_PREVIEW_COLUMNS is empty when running in tmux popup\nURL: https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/issues/4877\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n# $FZF_PREVIEW_COLUMNS is empty when running in tmux popup\n...\nI'm trying to create an interactive search / preview shortcut for tmux, it should let me search the current directory with ripgrep and show a preview of the current file using batcat.\n...\nCommand in .tmux.conf:\n`bind C-s display-popup -w 80% -h 80% -E -d \"#{pane_current_path}\" -T \"Search\" \"rg -n '' | fzf --delimiter=: --preview 'batcat --terminal-width=$FZF_PREVIEW_COLUMNS --highlight-line {2} --color=always {1}'\"`\n...\nI'm trying to set the terminal width for bat here, such that wrapping can work, otherwise long-ish lines wont be viewable.\n...\nHowever, `$FZF_PREVIEW_COLUMNS` seems to be set incorrectly as batcat complains that the value is ''. \n\n \n\n## Timeline\n...\n- Renamed from \"$$FZF_PREVIEW_COLUMNS is empty when running in tmux popup\" to \"$FZF_PREVIEW_COLUMNS is empty when running in tmux popup\"\n...\n> You should escape the variable (`\\$FZF_PREVIEW_COLUMNS`), otherwise it will be expanded before the command is executed.\n...\n> You might also want to check out the `--popup` (a.k.a. `--tmux`) option of fzf. Since 0.74.0, it uses a tmux floating pane instead of a popup (https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/releases/tag/v0.74.0).\n> \n> ```sh\n> # Use floating pane if available (tmux 3.7)\n> fzf --popup 80% --border-label ' Search '\n> \n> # Telling it to use popup instead by forcing fzf border\n> fzf --popup 80% --border-label ' Search ' --border\n> ```\n...\n> > You should escape the variable (`\\$FZF_PREVIEW_COLUMNS`), otherwise it will be expanded before the command is executed.\n> \n> That did the trick, thanks 👍🏻 \n> \n> \n> \n> > You might also want to check out the `--popup` (a.k.a. `--tmux`) option of fzf. Since 0.74.0, it uses a tmux floating pane instead of a popup (https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/releases/tag/v0.74.0).\n> > \n> > # Use floating pane if available (tmux 3.7)\n> > fzf --popup 80% --border-label ' Search '\n> > \n> > # Telling it to use popup instead by forcing fzf border\n> > fzf --popup 80% --border-label ' Search ' --border\n> \n> I thought about doing that, though that only works when triggering fzf from the command line. Currently I use a TMUX keybind to open a popup and call fzf, such that I can also do that on top of some other program. Also the closing behavior between the popup and floating pane differ a bit a the moment, so the popup still works better for my use case.\n...\n> You can use `--popup` in a tmux binding.\n> \n> ```\n> # Select pane\n> bind-key 0 run-shell -b \"tmux list-panes -a | fzf --reverse --style full --popup --delimiter : --bind 'enter:become:tmux select-pane -t {2}; tmux select-window -t {2}' || :\"\n> ```\n\n---\n\nTitle: Requires tmux 3.2 or above not only popup window · Issue #3959 · junegunn/fzf\nURL: https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/issues/3959\nPublished: 2024-08-08T00:00:00.000Z\nAuthor: junegunn\nHighlights:\n# Requires tmux 3.2 or above not only popup window #3959\n[New issue](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/issues/3959)\nCopy link\n[New issue](https://github.com/login?return_to=https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/issues/3959)\nCopy link\n...\n* Use fzf inside tmux\n```\nexport FZF_TMUX=1\n```\n* CTLR+R to call `\\_\\_fzf\\_history\\_\\_`\n* Choose command with ENTER or CTRL+C (or ESC)\n### Expected\n...\nReturn to terminal (tmux window) with command or empty command.\n### Result\n...\nIf using `tmux 3.0a` (latest version ubuntu 20.04) then process of return freezes (in both cases). After update tmux to `tmux 3.4` everything works as it should.\n### Problem\n...\nI looked a little to see what the reason might be. And found problem with command:\n```\ntmux split-window -c /home/username -l 40% 'bash -c '\\''exec -a fzf bash /tmp/fzf-args-3565'\\''' ';' set-option -p synchronize-panes off ';' set-option -p remain-on-exit off\n```\nHere:\n...\n[fzf/bin/fzf-tmux](https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/blob/c423c496a15b96cfc3c3fbd09135bcdc0c8e6b6e/bin/fzf-tmux#L239-L242)\nLines 239 to 242\nin\n...\n[c423c49](https://github.com/junegunn/fzf/commit/c423c496a15b96cfc3c3fbd09135bcdc0c8e6b6e)\n||tmux \\\\|\n|| split-window -c \"$PWD\"$opt\"bash -c 'exec -a fzf bash $argsf'\"$swap\\\\|\n||$tmux\\_off\\_opts\\\\|\n|| > /dev/null 2>&1 || { \"$fzf\"\"${args[@]}\"; exit $?; }|\n...\nFor `tmux 3.4` works well, for `tmux 3.0.a`:\n```\ncreate pane failed: -l invalid\n```\nWithout `%` for `-l` arg works well also (40 use as number of lines). So I think `tmux 3.0a` don't support percentage for `-l`.\n## Metadata\n## Metadata\n### Assignees\nNo one assigned\n### Labels",
