          "type": "text",
          "text": "Fixed. Two bugs, both specific to the tmux popup keybind (`bind g display-popup -E \"open-repo\"`):\n\n1. **Stuck popup**: `fzf --height=40%` uses alternate-screen sizing that conflicts inside `display-popup` — a known blank/frozen-popup regression with fzf 0.74.x + tmux 3.7 (junegunn/fzf#4845). Now the script detects popup context (`TMUX` set but `TMUX_PANE` unset) and runs fzf without `--height`, filling the popup cleanly.\n\n2. **Wrong cwd**: the old block ran `tmux display-message '#{pane_current_path}'` even from the popup, which resolves to the *active pane behind the popup* — I reproduced it opening the wrong repo. Now the `cd` only runs in a regular tmux pane; popups already start in the right directory via `-d \"#{pane_current_path}\"`.\n\nVerified all three modes end-to-end: plain shell ✓, normal tmux pane ✓, popup via your exact keybind mechanism ✓.",
