          "text": "Found it. The trace shows the script reaches `date +%s%N`, but the **journal has no systemd-run entry** — the popup closes the instant the script exits, killing the just-forked backgrounded `systemd-run` before it can register the unit with systemd. In a normal shell the parent terminal stays alive so the race never bites. Fix: don't background it — `systemd-run` already detaches into its own unit and returns immediately; and use `setsid --fork` for the fallback openers so they survive popup teardown too:",
